reviewer_concerns.value:
The reviewers initially raised several key concerns:

(1) strong and idealized assumptions, especially orthogonality and separability, with unclear robustness beyond toy or near orthogonal regimes;

(2) limited experimental validation and an unrealistic fine tuning setting that only adapts the classifier head, with missing or weak links to common multi layer LoRA use in attention blocks;

(3) insufficient evidence for practical relevance to LLMs and model merging practice, and requests for stronger comparisons and broader evaluations;

(4) clarity issues in presentation, including minor typos and definition distinctions noted by reviewers.
